  "title": "Annette Q NDE 6672",
  "date": "June 1986",
  "content": "I was taken into the hospital operating room to get control of the tetanus seizures [med: Tetanus is a serious bacterial disease that affects your nervous system, leading to painful muscle contractions, particularly of your jaw and neck muscles] that had re-occurred after taking medication. I was having major seizures and muscle spasms. I was given intravenous injections that were supposed to help, but that resulted in my going into total arrest [med. Cessation of both breathing and heartbeat.] I heard the two doctors and the nurses talking to each other, saying there was no movement on the monitors. They shocked me three times to try to get my heart going. While this struggle to get my body to respond was going on, I was watching them from above. I saw the doctor leave the operating room to go and tell my husband that it was all over. Meanwhile, I was experiencing an indescribable feeling of unconditional love and felt surrounded by the purest white light. The peace and love in which I was engulfed was simply too vast to be described in words. What I really wanted was to get lost in this peace and love. But, instead, I asked God, (an awesome presence that surrounded me) to let me go back. I said, ‘I have to go back, my baby is just over one year old and my other two daughters need me. I cannot stay here now.’ I awoke a week later in a different town, in the intensive care unit.",
